0..75 Comment "//! A type applies its family by juxtaposition, as a value call applies its"
76..89 Comment "//! function."
90..93 Comment "//!"
94..170 Comment "//! The floor spells a value call by juxtaposition, and a type now takes the"
171..241 Comment "//! same spelling. `Couple Integer (Maybe Integer)` is the application"
242..319 Comment "//! `Couple(Integer, Maybe(Integer))`. The call form reads as before, and the"
320..346 Comment "//! two spellings convert."
347..350 Comment "//!"
351..424 Comment "//! Each argument after the head is one operand, and parentheses group an"
425..500 Comment "//! argument that is an application. The application binds tighter than the"
501..577 Comment "//! returner and the arrow, so `-F Maybe A` returns `Maybe A`. A `(` after a"
578..655 Comment "//! space opens a group, and only a `(` directly after the head continues the"
656..717 Comment "//! call form. A lowercase head stays in the call form, as in"
718..788 Comment "//! `maybeRun(Integer)`. Its juxtaposed form `m T` is a type at a mode"
789..828 Comment "//! variable, which a later unit reads."
829..832 Comment "//!"
833..912 Comment "//! - see: #5326 — a type reads a juxtaposed application beside its call form"
913..972 Comment "//! - see: #5330 — the juxtaposed type at a mode variable"
974..1015 Comment "/// Optional values, `None` and `Some x`."
